⟁ .shadow — the real-life analog (the User behind the program)
node SPW · Scott Pilgrim vs. the World · ⟦The Katayanagi Twins:SPW:cf5fea⟧

think TRON: every program in the grid is cast from a User in the world outside it.
the carbon character is the program; this file is its User — the real-life analog
whose face and being the emergent is the digital shadow of.

the program (in-world) : The Katayanagi Twins — evil exes #5 & #6 · the robot-summoning DJs
the User (carbon)      : Shota & Keita Saito  [ the actor who lent the face ]
the analog (your world): the exes who fight you by proxy — rivals who never touch you, dueling through the machines and noise they command

the resemblance : The Saito twins barely speak; their power is the wall of electronic sound and the dragons it summons — opponents as pure synth.

the cast-line : the User stands in the carbon world; the program stands in the film;
                the shadow falls between them, and the credit returns to the human governor.
seal (program): We don't throw a single punch — we summon the dragons and let the synths do the fighting.

